9715223d7db1a4a23fbb18c89f54ceace121832f9a4531965f59b86cd5d73392{"version":1,"source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"},"layers":{"businessProfile":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"2a24b93983f9ab4fdc4062e62fb603c4e1a6a39a5cfcc358e4ee5b124baaadee","quote":"We commenced our express delivery service business through Shanghai Zhongtongji Express Service Co., Ltd. in Shanghai, China in January 2009. This entity operated express delivery services in Shanghai, Anhui Province, Jiangsu Province and Zhejiang Province, and authorized and cooperated with third-party business partners to operate ZTO-branded express delivery services elsewhere in China.","context":"A. History and Development of the Company","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":656,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"73b9774331055cc34a8dd401fe6a77f90fb7b0c9a27944caa1bb20369f9b29f0","quote":"In January 2013, the shareholders who owned Shanghai Zhongtongji Express Service Co., Ltd., together with 15 network partners located in the cities and provinces mentioned above, established ZTO Express as a holding company.","context":"We commenced our express delivery service business through Shanghai Zhongtongji Express Service Co., Ltd. in Shanghai, China in January 2009. This entity operated express delivery services in Shanghai, Anhui Province, Jiangsu Province and Zhejiang Province, and authorized and cooperated with third-party business partners to operate ZTO-branded express delivery services elsewhere in China.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":657,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"f92e5d23f3df4a371ce49013b09dc54ef237c7eab934d5a2efc2076932ad5cb7","quote":"In January 2014, ZTO Express acquired businesses and assets of Shanghai Zhongtongji Express Service Co., Ltd. and eight network partners that were wholly owned by some of the shareholders who formed ZTO Express.","context":"In January 2013, the shareholders who owned Shanghai Zhongtongji Express Service Co., Ltd., together with 15 network partners located in the cities and provinces mentioned above, established ZTO Express as a holding company.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":658,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"0a301da3291d4384cbe4f66eb43254fc5317260a76e2ff97e21ca5801a8d2d99","quote":"In October 2015, ZTO Express and its wholly owned subsidiaries acquired express delivery businesses from 16 network partners and their respective shareholders in exchange for equity interests in ZTO and cash.","context":"In January 2014, ZTO Express acquired businesses and assets of Shanghai Zhongtongji Express Service Co., Ltd. and eight network partners that were wholly owned by some of the shareholders who formed ZTO Express.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":659,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"843f133f6a5ebbe1f80f4cca4e4312dff11ae035336df3378a62477a11167b82","quote":"In April 2015, ZTO was incorporated under the laws of the Cayman Islands as our offshore holding company to facilitate financing and offshore listing. Upon its incorporation, ZTO issued 600,000,000 ordinary shares to the British Virgin Islands holding vehicles of the then shareholders of ZTO Express, in proportion to these shareholders’ then respective share percentage in ZTO Express. ZTO established ZTO Express Limited in British Virgin Islands as its wholly-owned subsidiary in April 2015. ZTO Express Limited subsequently established ZTO Express (Hong Kong) Limited as its wholly owned subsidiary in May 2015.","context":"In October 2015, ZTO Express and its wholly owned subsidiaries acquired express delivery businesses from 16 network partners and their respective shareholders in exchange for equity interests in ZTO and cash.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":660,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"6caad9d84d5ffa52e77caf794647dbcdbf55df2130d491b11da1d70ec7b08286","quote":"In July 2015, ZTO Express (Hong Kong) Limited established a wholly owned PRC subsidiary, Shanghai Zhongtongji Network. Due to the PRC legal restrictions on foreign ownership in companies that provide mail delivery services in China, we carry out our express delivery business through ZTO Express, a domestic PRC company, equity interests in which are held by PRC citizens and companies established in Shanghai China.","context":"In April 2015, ZTO was incorporated under the laws of the Cayman Islands as our offshore holding company to facilitate financing and offshore listing. Upon its incorporation, ZTO issued 600,000,000 ordinary shares to the British Virgin Islands holding vehicles of the then shareholders of ZTO Express, in proportion to these shareholders’ then respective share percentage in ZTO Express. ZTO established ZTO Express Limited in British Virgin Islands as its wholly-owned subsidiary in April 2015. ZTO Express Limited subsequently established ZTO Express (Hong Kong) Limited as its wholly owned subsidiary in May 2015.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":661,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"b1dd6a1de72298df72b0d9cde0bcde9f163cf0c6d1a0055964b25da9b513f8ca","quote":"Zhongtongji Network entered into a series of contractual arrangements, including an exclusive call option agreement, an equity pledge agreement, a voting rights proxy agreement, as described in more detail below, irrevocable powers of attorney and an exclusive consulting and services agreement and its supplemental agreement, with ZTO Express and its shareholders, and obtained spousal consent letters by the spouses of six key shareholders of ZTO Express. These shareholders are Messrs. Meisong Lai, Jianfa Lai, Jilei Wang, Xiangliang Hu, Shunchang Zhang and Xuebing Shang, collectively holding 73.8% of the equity interests in ZTO Express.","context":"In July 2015, ZTO Express (Hong Kong) Limited established a wholly owned PRC subsidiary, Shanghai Zhongtongji Network. Due to the PRC legal restrictions on foreign ownership in companies that provide mail delivery services in China, we carry out our express delivery business through ZTO Express, a domestic PRC company, equity interests in which are held by PRC citizens and companies established in Shanghai China.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":662,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"76a21693854fa9f3779397defb55e86623b659d551905e21b43a8286667ec9ac","quote":"As a result of these contractual arrangements, we are able to direct the activities of, and are the primary beneficiary of, ZTO Express. ZTO Express is therefore the consolidated affiliated entity, or the VIE, which generally refers to an entity in which we do not have any equity interests but whose financial results are consolidated into our consolidated financial statements in accordance with U.S. GAAP because we have effective financial control over, and are the primary beneficiary of, that entity. We treat ZTO Express and its subsidiaries as the consolidated affiliated entities under U.S. GAAP and have consolidated their financial results in our consolidated financial statements in accordance with U.S. GAAP. However, those contractual arrangements may not be as effective in providing us with the ability to direct the operational activities as direct ownership.","context":"Zhongtongji Network entered into a series of contractual arrangements, including an exclusive call option agreement, an equity pledge agreement, a voting rights proxy agreement, as described in more detail below, irrevocable powers of attorney and an exclusive consulting and services agreement and its supplemental agreement, with ZTO Express and its shareholders, and obtained spousal consent letters by the spouses of six key shareholders of ZTO Express. These shareholders are Messrs. Meisong Lai, Jianfa Lai, Jilei Wang, Xiangliang Hu, Shunchang Zhang and Xuebing Shang, collectively holding 73.8% of the equity interests in ZTO Express.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":663,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"8c9686217bdb816ae957913e67fec4dc7c8ac23c22f220ec7a099c4a88e938ed","quote":"On October 27, 2016, our ADSs commenced trading on the NYSE under the symbol “ZTO.” We raised from our initial public offering approximately $1.4 billion in net proceeds after deducting underwriting commissions and the offering expenses payable by us.","context":"As a result of these contractual arrangements, we are able to direct the activities of, and are the primary beneficiary of, ZTO Express. ZTO Express is therefore the consolidated affiliated entity, or the VIE, which generally refers to an entity in which we do not have any equity interests but whose financial results are consolidated into our consolidated financial statements in accordance with U.S. GAAP because we have effective financial control over, and are the primary beneficiary of, that entity. We treat ZTO Express and its subsidiaries as the consolidated affiliated entities under U.S. GAAP and have consolidated their financial results in our consolidated financial statements in accordance with U.S. GAAP. However, those contractual arrangements may not be as effective in providing us with the ability to direct the operational activities as direct ownership.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":664,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"234b04dcd68751271a247cc77f6f88d9a5c8204dd6c60a84156282efe4bade82","quote":"In May 2018, Alibaba and Cainiao Network entered into a strategic transaction with us. Pursuant to the transaction terms, investors led by Alibaba and Cainiao Network invested US$1.38 billion in our company in exchange for approximately 10% of our equity interest at that time and obtained certain shareholder rights in our company. The transaction was completed in June 2018.","context":"On October 27, 2016, our ADSs commenced trading on the NYSE under the symbol “ZTO.” We raised from our initial public offering approximately $1.4 billion in net proceeds after deducting underwriting commissions and the offering expenses payable by us.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":665,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"30cffb1d6adbcd8cf7407df39020df99e1aae960f4f2501b08facbca819d682f","quote":"In June 2018, we made a strategic investment of approximately US$168 million to acquire an approximately 15% equity stake in Cainiao Post, Cainiao Network’s network of last-mile delivery stations. Our strategic investment in Cainiao Post was done in conjunction with four other leading express delivery companies in China, including YTO Express, STO Express, Yunda Express, and Best Inc., in the aggregate amount of approximately US$495 million.","context":"In May 2018, Alibaba and Cainiao Network entered into a strategic transaction with us. Pursuant to the transaction terms, investors led by Alibaba and Cainiao Network invested US$1.38 billion in our company in exchange for approximately 10% of our equity interest at that time and obtained certain shareholder rights in our company. The transaction was completed in June 2018.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":666,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"4104dec1a0f78516873f3e9e450b79ba3ff52cdd980a003455c611017742664b","quote":"On September 29, 2020, our Class A ordinary shares commenced trading on the Main Board of the Hong Kong Stock Exchange under the stock code “2057.” We raised approximately HK$11.1 billion (US$1.4 billion) from the public offering of Class A ordinary shares in connection with our secondary listing in Hong Kong, after deducting underwriting commissions and the offering expenses payable by us.","context":"Table of Contents","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":669,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"8ccab951a109ee1f366aef5bd2d9d4295bc7ddb3b11ce3e14b1d4403a1664a89","quote":"On May 1, 2023, our voluntary conversion of our secondary listing status to primary listing on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange became effective, and ZTO became a dual-primary listed company on the Main Board of the Hong Kong Stock Exchange and the NYSE.","context":"On September 29, 2020, our Class A ordinary shares commenced trading on the Main Board of the Hong Kong Stock Exchange under the stock code “2057.” We raised approximately HK$11.1 billion (US$1.4 billion) from the public offering of Class A ordinary shares in connection with our secondary listing in Hong Kong, after deducting underwriting commissions and the offering expenses payable by us.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":670,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"3d1fbdc581632555c825dfbe10f353ef0e5eefc1393102c64661b1f381552922","quote":"Our principal executive offices are located at Building One, No.1685 Huazhi Road, Qingpu District, Shanghai, 201708, People’s Republic of China. Our telephone number at this address is +86 21 5980-4508. Our registered office in the Cayman Islands is located at the offices of Maples Corporate Services Limited, PO Box 309, Ugland House, Grand Cayman, KY1-1104, Cayman Islands. SEC maintains an internet site that contains reports, proxy and information statements, and other information regarding issuers that file electronically with the SEC on www.sec.gov. You can also find information on our website http://ir.zto.com. The information contained on our website is not a part of this annual report.","context":"On May 1, 2023, our voluntary conversion of our secondary listing status to primary listing on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange became effective, and ZTO became a dual-primary listed company on the Main Board of the Hong Kong Stock Exchange and the NYSE.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":671,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"33617379318682c2cc747cbc0a18c5df026b51c9553adbb0c679a6fde94a71d3","quote":"We are a leading express delivery company in China. Through our network and together with our network partners, we provide domestic and international express delivery services supplemented by other value-added services.","context":"B. Business Overview","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":673,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"da77c3da02509fcad7ff120deb2de7ac52f21053ace46c73db3a02bbf11673c5","quote":"We have developed an extensive and reliable delivery network in China. As of December 31, 2025, our network infrastructure consists of 93 sorting hubs with 596 automation lines, approximately 3,800 line-haul routes serviced by over 10,000 line-haul vehicles that we own and operate, and over 6,000 direct network partners operating over 31,000 pickup/delivery outlets and approximately 100,000 last-mile posts. Our network covers over 99% of cities and counties in China.","context":"We are a leading express delivery company in China. Through our network and together with our network partners, we provide domestic and international express delivery services supplemented by other value-added services.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":674,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"aed3c8ca0b98042df26a8394c2177056a0d9982b7e69a4deb81b8485cac5b298","quote":"Service Offerings by Us and Our Network Partners","context":"We have developed an extensive and reliable delivery network in China. As of December 31, 2025, our network infrastructure consists of 93 sorting hubs with 596 automation lines, approximately 3,800 line-haul routes serviced by over 10,000 line-haul vehicles that we own and operate, and over 6,000 direct network partners operating over 31,000 pickup/delivery outlets and approximately 100,000 last-mile posts. Our network covers over 99% of cities and counties in China.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":675,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"25db36acb7da88a637b17b916f6a99da290c5047c91e70a566dfad132adbe1d6","quote":"We mainly provide express deliveries in China of parcels weighing under 50 kilograms with expected delivery time ranging from 24 to 72 hours. Our delivery time has improved over time.","context":"Service Offerings by Us and Our Network Partners","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":676,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"9b3f974c0ec92f8ee7a5e42808260cc88797e691ec17cfae7e9215adc667ceb3","quote":"The following chart sets out the services provided by us and our network partners.","context":"We mainly provide express deliveries in China of parcels weighing under 50 kilograms with expected delivery time ranging from 24 to 72 hours. Our delivery time has improved over time.","section":"ITEM 4. INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":677,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-044613","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001677250","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1677250/000110465926044613/zto-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf.bin","sha256":"c857ec6939046ad06f222fd94451f136c4e34cef6873e4c6f844d667ea8defcf"}},{"id":"67379c3add8514d6f868d33176bd2f020faecb542450918b77e457938a2fb466","quote":"| | | | Key Category | ​ ​ ​ | | ​ ​ ​ | Service Offerings Domestic Express | | Express Delivery | |